Here is the commit message:
ACCUMULO-3784 fix getauths

Signed-off-by: Josh Elser <elserj@apache.org>

Here is the root cause:
The original implementation used a `SortedSet` to store authorizations, which may not have handled case-insensitive sorting correctly due to the way it was initialized and populated. This could lead to inconsistencies in the displayed authorizations for users, especially if the authorizations contained mixed-case letters. The refactoring to a `List` with explicit case-insensitive sorting addresses this issue directly.

